  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "# Complex Power Series and Analyticity [S+N]\n\nPower series in $\\mathbb{C}$ are like real ones, but with disks instead of intervals. A series $\\sum c_n (z - z_0)^n$ has a **radius of convergence** $R$ (Cauchy-Hadamard, same formula as in real analysis):\n\n$$\\frac{1}{R} = \\limsup_{n \\to \\infty} |c_n|^{1/n}.$$\n\nInside $\\{|z - z_0| < R\\}$ — the **disk of convergence** — the series converges absolutely. Outside, it diverges. On the boundary, behaviour is delicate.\n\nA function holomorphic on a disk equals its Taylor series there. We saw the hint in real analysis: $1/(1+x^2)$ has Taylor radius 1 because the complex singularities at $\\pm i$ are at distance 1. Now we can finally explain that.\n\nThis notebook states the link (holomorphic ⇔ analytic on disks) and its consequences; notebook 3.05 proves it.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "load(\"numerics\")$\nload(\"ax-plots\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 36,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Geometric series in $\\mathbb{C}$\n\n$\\sum_{n=0}^\\infty z^n = 1/(1 - z)$ for $|z| < 1$. The disk of convergence is the open unit disk; on the boundary $|z| = 1$ the series diverges (the terms don't go to zero).\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "z_test : 0.5 + 0.3 * %i$\nabs_z : float(cabs(z_test))$\nprint(\"z =\", z_test, \"  |z| =\", abs_z)$\nN : 50$\nrunning : 0.0 + 0.0*%i$\nfor n : 0 thru N do running : running + z_test^n$\nprint(\"Σ z^n (N=\", N, \"):\", expand(running))$\nprint(\"1/(1-z):\", rectform(1/(1 - z_test)))$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 37,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "z = 0.3*%i+0.5   |z| = 0.58309518948453\nΣ z^n (N= 50 ): 0.8823529411761379*%i+1.4705882352960256\n1/(1-z): 0.8823529411764707*%i+1.4705882352941178"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## Visualising the disk of convergence\n\nA power series converges on a disk and diverges outside it. Plot $|S_N(z)|$ for the geometric series at $N = 50$, using $S_N(z) = (1 - z^{N+1})/(1 - z)$ and squashing large values with $5\\tanh(|S_N|/5)$ so the figure stays readable. Inside the unit disk the surface stays low, rising only near $z = 1$ where the limit $1/(1-z)$ has its pole. Outside, $|z|^{51}$ grows fast and the surface climbs to the ceiling at $5$. The disk is a property of the series: the limit $1/(1-z)$ is finite everywhere except $z = 1$.\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* Partial sum S_50(z) = (1 - z^51)/(1 - z), squashed by 5·tanh(|S|/5):\n   about |S| for small values, flattening out near 5.  (min(|S|, 5) would be\n   simpler but is very slow to evaluate on a symbolic expression.)\n   Writing z = r e^{iθ} gives |1 - z^51|² = 1 - 2 r^51 cos(51θ) + r^102, which avoids\n   expanding (x + iy)^51 symbolically. */\nratprint : false$\nr_sq : x^2 + y^2$\nSN_mod : sqrt(1 - 2 * r_sq^(51/2) * cos(51 * atan2(y, x)) + r_sq^51)\n         / sqrt((1 - x)^2 + y^2)$\nax_draw3d(\n  explicit(5 * tanh(SN_mod / 5), x, -1.4, 1.4, y, -1.4, 1.4),\n  title=\"|S_50(z)| for Σ z^n (squashed at 5): low inside |z| < 1, saturated outside\",\n  xlabel=\"Re z\", ylabel=\"Im z\", zlabel=\"|S_50|\",\n  colorscale=\"Hot\"\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 38,
      "outputs": [
        {
